str.strip takes a SET of characters, not a suffix: 'glob.log'.strip('.log') returns 'b'. Write tests/test_cleanup.py first covering 'app.log' -> 'app', 'glob.log' -> 'glob', 'login.log' -> 'login', 'ollog.log' -> 'ollog', and a name without the suffix: 'readme' -> 'readme'. Run pytest, observe the carnage, then fix with str.removesuffix and only remove it once ('a.log.log' -> 'a.log'; test that). Also assert archive_name('glob.log', '2026-01-05') == 'glob-2026-01-05.gz' and finish with everything green.

